    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d766">

                <pb facs="1241" n="1227" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/1225: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-03T14:00:00+01:00">January 3, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 3—1:23 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4. Corcoran<anchor n="2" xml:id="d766-f1"/> states that pro-German Swede in
                    contact with German civilian and military officials who passed through Göteborg
                    states that high military officers have protested against German Government
                    proposal to hold mock trials of captured British and American airmen in reprisal
                    for Russian trials and execution of war guilty at Kharkov. German Propaganda
                    Ministry has been dissuaded from its original plan because there is definite
                    apprehension as to results of increasing public feeling against Allied airmen,
                    many of whom have been murdered by infuriated civilians when falling in German
                    territory after raids on German cities. Goebbels<anchor n="3" xml:id="d766-f2"/>
                    still urges that trials be held but military and naval offices advocate
                    cessation of all propaganda against Allied airmen. Repeated as my 5 to
                    London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d766-f1" n="2" xml:id="d766-f1-content">
                <p>William W. Corcoran, Consul General at Goteborg.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d766-f2" n="3" xml:id="d766-f2-content">
                <p>Joseph Goebbels, German Minister of Propaganda.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
